TAUREON Synth Tool V4 @VERSION@ — Windows x64 portable preview

Build revision: @REVISION@
Start TAUREON-Synth-Tool-V4.exe from this extracted folder. Keep its DLLs,
resources and plugin subdirectories together. Windows 11 x64 is the primary
target. No installer or automatic device configuration is provided.

WinMM uses native Windows MIDI support. The Windows MIDI Services (WMS) backend
targets the Windows MIDI Services Developer Preview 9 API (Windows.Devices.Midi2).
This ZIP does not contain Microsoft's preview API files, so WMS works only where
Windows provides that API or you place permitted API files beside the EXE.
Otherwise the Auto backend falls back to WinMM. Run
"TAUREON-Synth-Tool-V4.exe --list-midi wms" (or winmm) in this folder to list
routes or the initialization error without opening a MIDI port.

Real product-path MIDI/SysEx transfer and device restore have not yet passed
physical-hardware acceptance. Back up important synth data. Select exact RX/TX
routes deliberately and begin with receive/inspection workflows. Native display
scaling at 150% and 200% also remains to be checked.

Project, issues and source: https://github.com/sscheidl/TAUREON-Synth-Tool-V4
